{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Progress 2026-11-11 22:20 PST (session 3d705fec), worktree .rebar/worktrees/fix-milksnake.\nIncident trail (read-only grep of /var/gerrit/site/logs/httpd_log on i-00880b2c7f13527c5 via SSM, frontier profile): the 3344 run made exactly 3 Python-urllib/3.12 requests, all HTTP 200 — 03:55:04.357Z GET /a/changes/3344?o=CURRENT_REVISION&o=DETAILED_LABELS&o=SUBMITTABLE 200; 03:55:04.653Z POST /a/changes/3344/hashtags 200; 03:55:05.109Z POST /a/changes/3344/revisions/7a3baab7a2c6.../submit 200. No other urllib request for 3344 exists in any httpd_log. So the script's HTTP paths did not fail and its success path returns 0; the reported exit 1 is not attributable to Gerrit (most likely the calling shell; unrecoverable).\nFix (commit 5a4efd52a39): every post-vote exception path now reconciles. Submit non-409 HTTPError / URLError / OSError / ValueError -> re-read ?o=ALL_REVISIONS; MERGED with the submitted revision among its patch sets -> print merged, exit 0; else print error + Gerrit body, exit 1; failed re-read -> exit 1 naming both errors. Hashtag POST failures only warn. 409 path unchanged. RED first: the 7 new tests failed on the pre-fix script while the 25 existing tests passed; after the fix 32/32 pass. Lint (ratchets) and typecheck clean. make verify running."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794464047951806621,"uuid":"0ebeb605-75fd-42f9-b026-ddb2f0c0e515"}